    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my monstera deliciosa has been looking kinda rough lately. some of the lower leaves are turning a weird yellowish color and they feel a bit soft. i think i've been watering it about once a week but i'm not sure if that's too much or if it just needs more food? any idea what's going on?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing, soft lower leaves on a Monstera deliciosa can be a sign of a few things, but it often points to overwatering, which is a common issue with houseplant care. When the soil stays too soggy, the roots suffocate and start to rot, which leads to the leaves turning yellow and feeling mushy. I'd suggest letting the top couple of inches of soil dry out completely between waterings, rather than sticking to a strict weekly schedule. You could also check the drainage holes to make sure water isn't pooling underneath the pot.",
